    "text": "A point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> moves so that the sum of squares of its distances from the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be the locus of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, which intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></math>. Then the area of the quadrilateral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
